UID:5b53663635bb@paris-academique
DTSTAMP:20260527T165555Z
DTSTART:20260528T110000
DTEND:20260528T123000
SUMMARY:Framed polytopes and higher categories
DESCRIPTION:A framed polytope is the convex closure of a finite set of points in ℝⁿ together with an ordered linear basis. An n-category is a category that is enriched in the category of (n-1)-categories. Although these concepts may initially appear to be distant peaks in the mathematical landscape\, there exists a trail connecting them\, blazed in the 90's by Kapranov and Voevodsky. We will traverse this path\,\nhttps://indico.math.cnrs.fr/event/16556/
LOCATION:IHES
URL:https://indico.math.cnrs.fr/event/16556/
END:VEVENT
