SUMMARY:The motivic fundamental groupoid at tangential basepoints
DESCRIPTION:If U s a smooth scheme over a subfield of the field of complex numbers\, it is known from the work of Pierre Deligne and Alexander Goncharov that the prounipotent completion of the fundamental group of U based at any point has a motivic incarnation. More precisely\, its coordinate ring arises as the degree-zero homology of the Betti realization of a Hopf algebra object in Voevodsky's triangulated ca\nhttps://indico.math.cnrs.fr/event/16625/
