SUMMARY:A Central Limit Theorem for non identically distributed random variables with an application to Sobol indices
DESCRIPTION:The Central Limit Theorem (CLT) is one of the most well-known results in probability theory. It is traditionally stated for independent and identically distributed random variables. In this talk\, I will present a version of the Central Limit Theorem where we only keep the independence assumption. This generalization allows us to handle heterogeneous frameworks in statistics. I will then establish \nhttps://indico.math.cnrs.fr/event/16344/
