DTEND:20260604T150000
SUMMARY:Sections as a Computational Tool in Invariant Theory
DESCRIPTION:Invariants are essential for classifying mathematical objects up to a group of transformations. This talk will review several constructions of rational invariants where a section to the orbits is an essential ingredient for tractable computations. We will start with a general construction to obtain a generating set for the field of invariants. The output of the algorithm further provides rewrite r\nhttps://indico.math.cnrs.fr/event/16378/
LOCATION:IMT
URL:https://indico.math.cnrs.fr/event/16378/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:d35e284159b8@paris-academique
DTSTAMP:20260527T165555Z
DTSTART:20260604T140000
DTEND:20260604T160000
SUMMARY:A reduction from Hawk to the principal ideal problem in a quaternion algebra
DESCRIPTION:Hawk is a signature published in 2023\, whose security is based on a variant of the Lattice Isomorphism Problem\, called module-LIP. The publication of this signature sparked an interest in the resolution of module-LIP. In this talk\, we present a polynomial time reduction from this problem\, to another mathematical problem that involves quaternion algebras. This result comes from a 2025 paper of ours\nhttps://indico.math.cnrs.fr/event/16282/
LOCATION:IHP\, 11 rue Pierre et Marie Curie\, Paris 5e
URL:https://indico.math.cnrs.fr/event/16282/
END:VEVENT
